<title>ITALY: Italy Senate economic plan vote put off to Tuesday.</title>
<headline>Italy Senate economic plan vote put off to Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian Senate (upper house) will vote on the government's three-year economic target document (DPEF) next Tuesday, parliamentary party leaders said.</p>
<p>The Senate had been due to vote on the DPEF tomorrow, Friday, but acting upper house speaker Carlo Rognoni said the Senate would not be sitting tomorrow.</p>
<p>The house will begin debating the economic programme today as planned and will finish on Tuesday.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
